---
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
import Content from "../Content.astro";
import SectionHead from "../SectionHead.astro";
import Link from "../Link.astro";
import ProjectPubs from "../../layouts/ProjectPubs.astro";
import herbarium from "../../assets/img/herbarium.jpg";
import outreach from "../../assets/img/hh-lsu_outreach2.webp";
import softwareTraining from "../../assets/img/software-training-interns.jpg";
import labMentoring from "../../assets/img/leadership/lab-mentoring.jpg";
import FieldworkMap from "../map/FieldworkMap";
import FieldTraining from "./FieldTraining.astro";
import { expeditions } from "../../scripts/fieldwork";

const collecting = expeditions.filter((e) => e.kind === "collecting");
const collectingCountries = new Set(collecting.map((e) => e.country)).size;

const pillars = [
  {
    title: "Specimen acquisition",
    text: "Targeted fieldwork in under-sampled biodiversity hotspots across the Indo-Australian Archipelago, using best practices for specimen and tissue preservation while linking photographs and recordings to voucher specimens directly in the field.",
  },
  {
    title: "Stewardship & data",
    text: [
      { text: "FAIR", url: "https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/" },
      " data, ready for ",
      { text: "Darwin Core", url: "https://dwc.tdwg.org/" },
      " and ",
      { text: "Frictionless Data", url: "https://frictionlessdata.io/" },
      " from the field onward. NAHPU, our cross-platform digital field catalog, supports QR/barcode scanning and is adding automatic validation to streamline data flow from field to collection database.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Training & outreach",
    text: "Collecting while training local students closest to the field sites, and explicitly crediting the communities, guides, and porters who make remote expeditions possible.",
  },
];
---

<div>
  <SectionHead
    text="Biodiversity Inventories: Building Natural History Collections"
  />
  <Content>
    <p>
      Continuously growing collections keep natural history museums relevant:
      newly acquired specimens are the best material for genomic, microbiome,
      and phenomic studies, and many regions remain poorly documented. Over 13
      years, my work has both drawn on existing museum collections and built new
      ones, expanding sampling to under-surveyed islands and mountains.
    </p>
  </Content>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    {
      pillars.map((p) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-moss-900/15 bg-white p-4 dark:border-moss-100/15 dark:bg-forest-950">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-forest-900 dark:text-forest-100">
            {p.title}
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-forest-800 dark:text-forest-200">
            {typeof p.text === "string"
              ? p.text
              : p.text.map((part) =>
                  typeof part === "string" ? (
                    part
                  ) : (
                    <Link text={part.text} url={part.url} />
                  ),
                )}
          </p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <SectionHead text="Field collecting localities" />
  <figure>
    <FieldworkMap kind="collecting" client:visible />
    <figcaption class="mt-3 text-pretty text-sm text-forest-700 dark:text-forest-300">
      Localities from {collecting.length} field collecting expeditions in {collectingCountries} countries. Larger markers show repeat visits. For all fieldwork, including biodiversity surveys, see the <a href="/fieldwork" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-mist-700 underline hover:text-mist-900 dark:text-mist-200 dark:hover:text-mist-100">Fieldwork page</a>.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <SectionHead text="Field mammalogy training" />
  <Content>
    <p>
      My fieldwork has a dual intent: to study mammals in poorly surveyed regions, and to train students who live closest to those habitats. In collaboration with the Indonesian Research and Innovation Agency (<Link text="BRIN" url="https://www.brin.go.id/" />), we invited two undergraduates from the areas closest to our field sites to join our 2023 Sumatra expeditions. They started by measuring specimens and took on harder tasks each week, working alongside experienced mammalogists until they could prepare specimens on their own and help run the expedition.
    </p>
  </Content>
  <FieldTraining />

  <SectionHead text="Software development training" />
  <Content>
    <p>
      Computer science students are more often exposed to medical applications than to biodiversity science. With support from the <Link text="Florida Museum" url="https://www.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/" /> Undergraduate Internship Program, I train computer science undergraduates in software development for biodiversity research. They learn software architecture, practice on the large codebase of <Link text="BioCosmos" url="https://github.com/BioVisionLab/BioCosmos" />, and use programming and data science to study large museum collection datasets.
    </p>
  </Content>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <Image
      src={labMentoring}
      alt="Heru walking students through code and results on a monitor"
      widths={[400, 800]}
      sizes="(min-width: 640px) 50vw, 100vw"
      class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-xl object-cover object-[50%_35%]"
    />
    <Image
      src={softwareTraining}
      alt="Two interns at a desk reviewing code and a chart on a large monitor"
      class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-xl object-cover"
    />
  </div>

  <SectionHead text="Public engagement" />
  <Content>
    <Image
      src={outreach}
      alt="Giving an outreach presentation at the LSU Museum of Natural Science"
      width={300}
      class="float-left mb-2 mr-4 mt-2 rounded-xl"
    />
    <p>
      Museums are critical interfaces between scientific discovery and public
      literacy. At outreach events, such as those at the LSU Museum of Natural
      Science, I share representative specimens from our collections and the
      tools we use in the field. Engagement also continues in the field, with
      the local communities who make our expeditions possible.
    </p>
  </Content>
  <div class="clear-both"></div>

  <Image
    src={herbarium}
    alt="Herbarium Universitas Andalas"
    width={220}
    class="rounded-xl float-right ml-4 mt-8"
  />
  <SectionHead text="Herbarium digitization and data mobilization" />
  <Content>
    <p>
      This project is led by Dr. Nurainas at the Herbarium Universitas Andalas
      (ANDA) funded through the collection and data mobilization grant provided
      by the Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF). We digitized
      >65,000 sheets of the herbarium specimens at ANDA and make the data
      accessible through the GBIF portal.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 mb-2 text-semibold">Published datasets:</div>
    <ProjectPubs ids={["nurainas2024a", "nurainas2024b", "nurainas2024c"]} />
  </Content>
</div>
